  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Light-Regent Xouhoulong (beacon-lit) chang'Rampart
    
    ### Station and Rise
    
    Light-Regent of Aurora Stack and leader of The Icebound Exchange, the merchant guild controlling Aurora Stack's trade routes, during the Faction Wars. Xouhoulong rose from the tutelage of High-Beak Auditor Selka, the Exchange's previous leader, and was also trained by Grand Auditor Qeihong (tide-touched) of the High Tier — who would eventually displace him. His epithet marks him as a beacon-keeper by original training: a crystal-worker, not a politician. The scars on his flippers confirm this — fine white conduction-burns across the webbing from aurora-work performed before he learned restraint.
    
    He practiced The Shell Hatch, a krill-bloom mapping technique whose aurora-crystal resonance erodes recent memory, and was among practitioners reported unable to remember their own children.
    
    ### Works and Consolidation
    
    Xouhoulong designed the Hearth Plaza's upper galleries with mathematical precision, each crystal spire angled to channel aurora-radiance through the concentric trade-floors. He built the Exchange beyond anything Selka intended — less a trade collective, more a mechanism for consolidating resource-flow under a single authority.
    
    ### The Foedus∴vincu and the Deep Chambers
    
    Two decisions define Xouhoulong's tenure, and the ice preserves both.
    
    First: the Foedus∴vincu, a compact granting orca raiders known as The Midnight Claws diplomatic access to the Berg's deep tunnels as "honored guests" in exchange for fleet protection. Xouhoulong pressed the Directrix Mirror to the document himself. My annotation on Vel'keth the Younger notes that at least one orca leader sought Xouhoulong specifically because he "would trade what was not his to trade." The ice confirms the assessment.
    
    Second: in galleries beneath the Hearth Plaza that appeared on no official schematic, he commissioned research into deep-ice pressure-magic — spiral channels carved into ancient ice, fed with blood and invocation. ☽'ofund' Guild researchers and his own aurora-readers collaborated until something answered and two researchers vanished through a breach the ice carved on its own. When Qeihong investigated, Xouhoulong cited Mandatum∴absconditu — a Nightshelf doctrine of concealed authority with no jurisdiction over an Aurora Stack Light-Regent. That he reached for it tells us more than the citation itself.
    
    ### The Calving and Displacement
    
    Three weeks later, the Calving tore open the Berg's eastern face. Selka was in the eastern galleries. She did not survive.
    
    The Wake-Singers, a cult of orca shamans devoted to waking their dead god, followed — their hymns propagating through the very crystal geometry Xouhoulong had designed. He sealed the southern gallery himself, his old burns splitting open as he worked aurora-glass and ice-weld. Qeihong displaced him shortly after. He accepted it with what witnesses describe as measured grace.
    
    ### Afterward
    
    He never visited Selka's ice-memorial. He moved her commendation plaque from the antechamber to the vault because he could not work beneath her gaze. During one Long Dark — when the boundary between living and dead thins — her ghost stood near him for three hours. He did not look at her. Her claim remains open, unfiled.
    
    He keeps a bone carving taken from a Wake-Singer corpse during the Vum∴tenebra, depicting something vast moving beneath the ice. Before dawn, when no one is awake, he stands before it and does not move.
    
    The early ice-memory near the Hearth Plaza preserves a younger penguin's silhouette ringed in light that was not aurora-glow. The colony historians learned not to ask about it.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771576062132_0", anchor: "among practitioners reported unable to remember their own children", text: "\"Reported.\" By whom? The Shell Hatch literature is almost entirely written by non-practitioners summarizing what they observed from outside. Memory erosion is invisible to witnesses — you see a penguin stare blankly at a chick and infer the rest. Whether Xouhoulong had children to forget is a question no source I found thought to ask.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771576062132_1", anchor: "Xouhoulong cited Mandatum∴absconditu — a Nightshelf doctrine of concealed authority with no jurisdiction over an Aurora Stack Light-Regent", text: "One does not reach for foreign legal precedent in a crisis unless one has studied it at leisure. The question worth asking is not why he cited it but when he learned it, and from whom on the Nightshelf he expected to honor the claim. Shadow-Broker Nyla's predecessor was Aurora-born — I have noted this elsewhere. The channels existed.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771576062132_2", anchor: "He never visited Selka's ice-memorial", text: "I wrote on the Exchange entry what the eastern gallery ice preserves about them: body-heat signatures consistent with nesting, not ambiguous, not \"in some accounts.\" Read this passage with that knowledge. He did not avoid the memorial out of indifference. He avoided it the way a beacon-keeper avoids staring into the prism — you do not look directly at what will blind you. Her claim remains open because filing it would require someone to name what she was to him, and the Exchange's succession records cannot absorb that without unraveling three appointments.", type: :commentary, display: :full
